1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
<font color="#20e020">HI removed, cleaned
and corrected by Lunar Team</font>

2
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:24,189
Girls were last seen leaving
Sullivan's Tavern at 1:00 in the morning.

3
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:28,193
A truck driver spotted the car around 5:30
and called it in.

4
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:30,529
Look, I only have four deputies.

5
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:34,241
Only a couple of them
have ever seen a body killed in anger.

6
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:37,870
If what we have here is a homicide,
I'm gonna need some help.

7
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:41,040
Just to be clear,
except in special circumstances...

8
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:45,127
...we don't help out, we take over.
You need to be okay with that.

9
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:48,756
Okay. I guess.

10
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:52,509
She's not really a morning person.

11
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:54,803
She'll improve.

12
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:56,638
Names of the missing women?

13
00:00:56,806 --> 00:00:59,224
Nicole Gilbert and Kara Palmer.

14
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:03,270
Local girls. Both 21.
Work together in a hunting store in town.

15
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,565
Last night
was Nicole's engagement party.

16
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:10,944
- The car was found exactly like this?
- Yup... Well, no.

17
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:13,989
Uh, the door was open just like that.
We popped the trunk.

18
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:23,999
Yup, dead as a dodo. No gas either.
They must have left it running.

19
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:26,668
A different set of tire tracks
pulled off the road.

20
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:28,670
A truck or a big SUV, looks like.

21
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:33,759
They're still fresh. Must be from the trucker
who called in the car.

22
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:37,846
- Make sure Forensics gets a mold.
- Yep.

23
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:40,933
What's going on with your dog?

24
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:44,603
He's confused somehow. This behavior?

25
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:48,649
He's saying, "Hey, look, here they are.
Give me my Slim Jim already."

26
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:51,360
Parker, do you have a better dog
close by somewhere?

27
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:54,696
Sir, this is the best dog in the county.

28
00:01:54,864 --> 00:01:57,366
Come on, Dexter.
People are waiting on us.

29
00:01:57,534 --> 00:01:59,952
- Did you look under the car?
- Under the car?

30
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,621
- Yeah.
- Of course, we looked under the car.

31
00:02:10,463 --> 00:02:12,714
Oh, crap.

32
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:15,008
One or two?

33
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,971
One.

34
00:02:20,723 --> 00:02:22,516
It's Kara Palmer.

35
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:26,311
So where's Nicole Gilbert?

36
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:30,107
Nicole!

37
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:33,569
Good boy, Dexter.
He's got her on lock now.

38
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:36,655
Any way to tell from the scent
how fast Nicole was moving?

39
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:39,241
Oh, sure. Dexter's detecting skin cells.

40
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:42,578
They fall off your body all the time
at a pretty consistent rate.

41
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:46,623
- The faster you move, the thinner the trail.
- So are we following Nicole on foot...

42
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:49,668
- ...or Nicole tied up in the back of a truck?
- I don't know.

43
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:52,045
You said you could tell
how fast she was moving.

44
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:54,464
Dexter can tell.
I'm just walking behind him.

45
00:02:54,632 --> 00:02:57,426
- Nicole, can you hear us?
- Tell us about Kara and Nicole.

46
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:01,555
Known them practically their whole lives.
Kara was a real sweetheart.

47
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:04,766
You'll find no one here
who'll say a bad word of Kara Palmer.

48
00:03:04,934 --> 00:03:08,937
- Good church-going family. No trouble at all.
- Meaning Nicole Gilbert was trouble?

49
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:13,775
Nicole, well, she had her problems.
Drugs and drug-related foolishness mostly.

50
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:16,445
- Fraud, petty theft.
- Any violent offenses?

51
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:21,366
No, no. She was more of a
troubled soul than a bad person. Tough life.

52
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:26,121
Her mom died when she was 7.
Her father raised her on meth and hot dogs.

53
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:29,291
He's in prison now for drug dealing.

54
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:32,920
Kara and her family
were all the stability Nicole ever had.

55
00:03:33,087 --> 00:03:36,215
So she and Kara were good friends.
Odd match.

56
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:38,467
Real close since they were little.

57
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:40,844
In a small town,
you don't choose your friends.

58
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:44,806
They're the same age, they're female.
That's enough.

59
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:50,145
- Kyle. Boys, thank you for coming.
- Sheriff. Where do you want us?

60
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:53,815
You know this valley as well as anyone.
Just pick your spots.

61
00:03:53,983 --> 00:03:57,444
- Do we know if she's armed?
- What do you know about this case?

62
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:59,446
Uh, same thing as everybody else,
I guess.

63
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:04,618
Badass townie girl got drunk, stabbed her
friend to death, and ran off into the woods.

64
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:07,996
Kara Palmer died from loss of blood.
Nicole Gilbert is missing.

65
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:11,500
Maybe she ran off,
maybe she was abducted. We don't know.

66
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:13,502
Don't assume anything.

67
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:17,631
Message received and understood, ma'am.
All right, fellas.

68
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:23,303
- You knew Nicole, you think she did this?
- Who knows what others are capable of?

69
00:04:23,596 --> 00:04:26,306
She sure had built up a lot of bad karma.
But I don't know.

70
00:04:26,474 --> 00:04:30,519
- She seemed to be turning her life around.
- Bad karma doesn't have an expiration date.

71
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:33,313
Uh, actually, it does.

72
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:37,484
According to traditional Buddhist teachings.
I'm counting on it.

73
00:04:40,655 --> 00:04:42,322
Let's go.

74
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:06,179
People in town are already saying
Nicole did this. But I don't believe it.

75
00:05:07,181 --> 00:05:12,227
She will have to tell me herself
that she did this, before I believe it.

76
00:05:15,606 --> 00:05:16,815
Nicole loved our daughter.

77
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:19,776
And we loved Nicole
almost like she was our own.

78
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:23,572
- Well, almost.
- Why? Why would she kill her?

79
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:27,117
She had her troubles, Lord knows,
but she wasn't crazy.

80
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:29,995
Has there been any tension
between them recently? Nothing.

81
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:33,915
- No. None at all.
- Well...

82
00:05:34,709 --> 00:05:38,670
- Yes?
- That boy, that fiancé of Nicole's?

83
00:05:38,838 --> 00:05:40,422
Jason O'Toole.

84
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:43,592
We never met him but once or twice,
and he seemed nice enough.

85
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,927
He works lumber.
You know how those fellas are.

86
00:05:46,095 --> 00:05:49,014
Like to play the buck.
All but sleep at Sullivan's Tavern.

87
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:52,100
But, you know, these days
you have to look past the piercings...

88
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:56,772
...and the tattoos and all that, don't you?
But Kara didn't think much of him.

89
00:05:56,939 --> 00:05:59,024
- No?
- Didn't approve.

90
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:03,028
- There might have been some tension there.
- What was her problem with Jason?

91
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:07,449
I guess, just a feeling
that he wasn't trustworthy, you know?

92
00:06:07,825 --> 00:06:10,952
But Nicole was in love
and she thought Kara was just jealous.

93
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:14,456
- Kara didn't have a boyfriend.
- Did Jason ever get violent with Nicole?

94
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,708
Not that I heard,
but I wouldn't be surprised.

95
00:06:16,876 --> 00:06:19,378
Nicole's had her fair share of that type.

96
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:24,132
- Kara didn't have a boyfriend?
- Kara could have had anyone she liked.

97
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:29,429
She had no shortage of suitors.
But have you seen the men round here?

98
00:06:29,847 --> 00:06:34,226
It's all drunken lumberjacks
and hippie pot farmers.

99
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:36,103
Kara had...

100
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,940
She had higher standards than that.

101
00:06:49,992 --> 00:06:52,452
What's the problem now, Parker?

102
00:06:53,496 --> 00:06:55,664
Trail's cold, sheriff.

103
00:06:56,165 --> 00:06:58,333
Best dog in the county, huh?

104
00:06:59,168 --> 00:07:00,961
Come on, Dexter.

105
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:07,342
Nicole!

106
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,430
She can't answer you.

107
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:12,848
Or doesn't want to.

108
00:07:13,015 --> 00:07:16,601
- Nope, she's a captive, or dead.
- How do you know that?

109
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:19,980
How far have we come? What, five miles?

110
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:24,025
Nicole would have been barefoot,
probably drunk. It was a dark night.

111
00:07:24,193 --> 00:07:27,654
No way she could cover that distance.
Someone must have her in a vehicle.

112
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:31,992
- And Dexter lost the scent.
- Okay, you're in charge. What do we do?

113
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:35,537
Close to evening. Call off the search.
Gather everybody together and...

114
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:38,165
Give up? There's a girl missing.

115
00:07:38,332 --> 00:07:41,585
Tell me, of the men on this search party,
which one would you guess...

116
00:07:41,752 --> 00:07:44,671
- ...is a violent sexual predator?
- What kind of question...?

117
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:47,299
Whose name just popped into your head?
Someone's did.

118
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,009
Huh, there's always someone.

119
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:52,888
This is your method?
Asking people to guess who done it?

120
00:07:53,055 --> 00:07:55,015
Strange kind of detective work
you guys do.

121
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:59,144
Jane's being dramatic. But if somebody did
victimize Kara and Nicole...

122
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:02,147
...statistics show they'd be likely
to join the search party.

123
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:05,567
They enjoy the deceit.
It's like being the invisible man.

124
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:07,319
- Is that right?
- Yeah.

125
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:10,947
So gather up the search party,
let me have a crack at them.

126
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:13,992
He gets results.

127
00:08:14,577 --> 00:08:16,661
I know all these guys.

128
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:18,413
I'll vouch for every one of them.

129
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,542
Well, most of them.

130
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:31,927
I'll call them in.

131
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:45,023
- Jason O'Toole?
- Get your truck out of my way.

132
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:46,942
We need to talk about Nicole Gilbert.

133
00:08:47,109 --> 00:08:50,028
- I don't have time for this, guys.
- Let's have a little chat.

134
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:55,075
Where were you going
in such a hurry, Jason?

135
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:58,620
- Back to the woods to find Nicole.
- How do you know she was in the woods?

136
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:00,789
I don't. I hope she's in the woods.

137
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:04,251
Because if she's not in the woods,
she could be anywhere in the world.

138
00:09:04,418 --> 00:09:08,129
- Why not search with the rest of the town?
- I cover more ground alone.

139
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:10,632
Why did Kara drive Nicole home?
Why didn't you?

140
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,718
- Because I was too drunk.
- Or maybe you two had a fight?

141
00:09:13,886 --> 00:09:17,973
- No. We were celebrating our engagement.
- That's right about when the fights start.

142
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:21,476
We videoed the whole thing.
You can watch and see. There's no fighting.

143
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:24,396
- We'll do that. Where is that video?
- It's in my truck.

144
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:27,649
There's this whole Kara issue
we have to talk about.

145
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:29,651
- Maybe that blew up, huh?
- What issue?

146
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:33,071
Kara didn't like you. Didn't think
you were good enough for Nicole.

147
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:36,032
- Thought you were untrustworthy.
- That's funny.

148
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:39,995
Is that what you do? Try to get me all upset
or something, so I look guilty?

149
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:42,330
Does it upset you?
That Kara didn't like you?

150
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:46,001
- She was trying to undermine you?
- I couldn't care less, okay?

151
00:09:46,168 --> 00:09:48,336
Because it's not true anyhow.

152
00:09:48,504 --> 00:09:52,007
Kara liked me well enough.
At least, I never heard her say different.

153
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:54,759
Where were you between
1 and 7 a.m. last night?

154
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:01,016
I was here. Passed out on the floor.

155
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:10,108
We'll regroup in the morning, first light.

156
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:15,363
Before you go, Patrick Jane from the CBI,
would like to have a word with all of you.

157
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,824
Thanks, Sheriff Nelson.

158
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:23,955
I want you to look at me, all of you.
And listen closely.

159
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:27,709
I'd like you to raise your hands
above your heads like this.

160
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:31,713
Both hands.

161
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:34,466
You too, sheriff.

162
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:37,302
And you, Agent Lisbon.

163
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:40,930
Please.

164
00:10:43,309 --> 00:10:44,851
Good. Very good. One of you...

165
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:48,355
One of you here killed Kara Palmer
and abducted Nicole Gilbert.

166
00:10:48,522 --> 00:10:51,816
I want that person
to lower their right hand now.

167
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:03,578
Uh, okay, okay. Uh, it usually gets a hit.

168
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:06,748
Forget I even spoke.

169
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:11,836
Sheriff, we have
a 10-28 reported on Nicole Gilbert.

170
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:16,424
At the gas station convenience store.
I repeat, 10-28 on Nicole Gilbert.

171
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:17,926
Copy that.

172
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:30,814
She had a nasty blow to her head.

173
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:33,566
A moderate concussion.
Her feet are badly abraded.

174
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:37,987
And she has a lot of minor scratches
and bruises. Mild hypothermia.

175
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:43,660
Physically, she'll be fine in a day or so.
Mentally, it's another story.

176
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:47,914
When you brought her in,
she was in some kind of a psychotic state.

177
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:50,625
We've medicated her
to take the edge off that.

178
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:52,836
But she's still in deep shock.

179
00:11:53,003 --> 00:11:55,797
She has no memory at all of the events
that brought her here.

180
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,132
That's convenient.

181
00:11:57,299 --> 00:12:00,844
If I'd just stabbed my best friend to death,
I'd wanna forget too.

182
00:12:01,011 --> 00:12:03,805
Soon as she's well, I'm charging her
and taking her to jail.

183
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:08,476
Sheriff, you have custody of Nicole,
but the CBI is leading this investigation.

184
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:10,228
I decide when to file charges.

185
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:14,065
- We don't have the full facts yet.
- Facts? She's covered in blood.

186
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:16,317
Carrying what looks to be
the murder weapon...

187
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:19,028
...which the forensic guys say
has Kara's blood on it.

188
00:12:19,488 --> 00:12:21,531
What more do you want?

189
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:23,992
Is she well enough to speak to?

190
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:26,745
As long as you're gentle with her.

191
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:34,627
- Have you told her Kara's dead?
- No. We don't wanna upset her.

192
00:12:34,795 --> 00:12:37,505
- She's very fragile.
- Yeah.

193
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:43,595
Nicole?

194
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:46,598
My name's Teresa Lisbon.

195
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:49,225
I'm with the California Bureau
of Investigation.

196
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:51,519
- Hi.
- I wanna ask you a few questions...

197
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:53,521
...about what happened to you and Kara.

198
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:56,107
I told the doctor, I can't remember.

199
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:58,067
That's okay.

200
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,361
What's the last thing you do remember?

201
00:13:01,238 --> 00:13:02,530
My party.

202
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:07,202
I remember leaving Sullivan's
and getting in the car with Kara.

203
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:10,747
You know where my fiancé is?

204
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:13,249
Do you remember anything else
about the party?

205
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:17,545
- We had a good time.
- Nothing bad or unusual happen?

206
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:21,216
No. We drank a lot.

207
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:24,093
Danced.

208
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:26,763
Where's Kara?

209
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:33,019
You and Kara left the Sullivan in her car.
Then what happened?

210
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:35,271
I don't know.

211
00:13:36,273 --> 00:13:41,152
I don't know. That's what I'm telling you.
Next thing I remember, I was in this bed.

212
00:13:43,447 --> 00:13:46,157
What's wrong with me? What happened?

213
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:48,993
- Where's Kara? Why won't anyone tell me?
- It's okay.

214
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:51,663
- She's dead.
- Jane.

215
00:13:51,831 --> 00:13:53,665
Stabbed to death.

216
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:59,587
No. No, no.

217
00:14:00,589 --> 00:14:01,756
Why did you say that?

218
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:05,260
- She was gonna find out at some point.
- The doctor said to be gentle.

219
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:07,095
Ah, doctors.

220
00:14:09,014 --> 00:14:11,432
Open your eyes, Nicole.

221
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:13,977
Look at me.

222
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:16,271
Open your eyes.

223
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:23,611
I told you the truth
because you can handle it.

224
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:26,322
You have to. You will.

225
00:14:30,035 --> 00:14:31,369
Tell me you will.

226
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:38,251
What you have to do now,
you have to remember what happened.

227
00:14:40,337 --> 00:14:42,964
- Close your eyes and remember.
- Jane.

228
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:45,216
Close your eyes.

229
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:51,097
You were driving with Kara
down Flagship Road.

230
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:53,016
- Pull over.
- What?

231
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:55,143
Pull over.

232
00:14:55,311 --> 00:15:00,231
- Why did you stop?
- I was feeling sick.

233
00:15:02,484 --> 00:15:03,651
Hey.

234
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:10,491
- There's a man.
- What does he look like?

235
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:13,077
I don't know. I can't see. It's dark.

236
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:19,250
I can hear a loud rushing sound.

237
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,836
Like water.

238
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:28,092
Then what happened?

239
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:31,554
I don't know.

240
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:34,098
- I can't remember.
- You have to.

241
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:38,186
- I can't.
- You have to.

242
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:39,896
I can't remember.

243
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,522
- You have to.
- I can't.

244
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:44,859
What have you been doing to her? Out.

245
00:15:56,747 --> 00:15:59,415
That's bull.
She's got amnesia, but not so badly...

246
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:03,461
...she can't finger somebody else
for killing Kara? Rushing water, my ass.

247
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:06,881
No. She's telling the truth.
Something happened.

248
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:09,550
Something too horrible
for her mind to handle.

249
00:16:09,718 --> 00:16:12,762
- Her memory's blocked.
- Even if that's true, maybe it's blocked...

250
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:15,223
- ...because she killed Kara.
- Well, it's possible.

251
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:19,102
- I don't think so. I think she's a victim.
- How can you tell?

252
00:16:23,273 --> 00:16:24,565
It's in her eyes.

253
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:26,442
Oh.

254
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:30,405
Well, then. Why didn't you say so?
It's in her eyes.

255
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:34,117
Here's me looking for facts.

256
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:37,745
Why would she kill her best friend?
What's her, uh, motive?

257
00:16:37,913 --> 00:16:40,623
- Why do women kill other women?
- Over men.

258
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:44,252
Could have been fighting over Jason,
though he's no Brad Pitt.

259
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,587
- She was covered in blood.
- Yes?

260
00:16:46,755 --> 00:16:50,008
But it rained. It rained hard
for a good few hours last night.

261
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:54,262
Only, when they recovered Nicole,
she was still covered in blood. So...

262
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:57,140
She must have been under cover.
She must have been indoors.

263
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:59,142
- She was hiding.
- Or she was a captive.

264
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:03,312
Probably, near the river.
Hence, the sound of rushing water.

265
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:09,986
- Rigsby.
- Get park rangers and organize a search...

266
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:14,657
...of the summer cabins, storage units and
sheds within earshot of the river. Caves too.

267
00:17:14,825 --> 00:17:19,287
Oh, and have Van Pelt set up the video
Jason shot of the party at Sullivan's Tavern.

268
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:20,455
You got it, boss.

269
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:23,541
- Let's go.
- Mm. Uh, sheriff?

270
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:27,378
A man out there needs to silence Nicole
before she recovers her memory.

271
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:30,006
- So you say.
- So I say.

272
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:34,010
No one should enter her room.

273
00:17:34,636 --> 00:17:36,387
Make sure your men keep her safe.

274
00:17:36,972 --> 00:17:39,182
- I know my business.
- Yeah.

275
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:42,894
You mind yours.
Whatever in the heck it is.

276
00:17:52,654 --> 00:17:54,155
How's Jason's alibi look?

277
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:57,492
Alibi's solid. Several people saw him
passed out at the bar.

278
00:17:57,659 --> 00:18:00,536
- Damn. Nelson was right.
- About what?

279
00:18:00,704 --> 00:18:04,999
Look at Jason's camera work.
He's torn between Nicole and Kara.

280
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:08,336
- I love this girl. I love this girl.
- And I love you, baby.

281
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:11,881
He had a thing for Kara. There's no proof
of a motive unless Nicole knew.

282
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:14,509
Doesn't look like
they're feuding over him, does it?

283
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:16,010
I'm getting married!

284
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:20,264
Wait. Stop right there. Run it back.

285
00:18:21,183 --> 00:18:25,353
There. The guy at the bar staring at Kara,
in the baseball cap.

286
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:28,106
I can blow it up.

287
00:18:29,566 --> 00:18:31,901
Let's get a better look at that hat.

288
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:36,364
"Earthly Pure." What is that?

289
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:39,951
That's the brand of cosmetics
we found in Kara's vehicle.

290
00:18:41,411 --> 00:18:43,621
Can we match that image
to the DMV database?

291
00:18:43,789 --> 00:18:44,872
I can try.

292
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:54,215
"Rulon Farnes."

293
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:05,810
Truck driver for Earthly Pure Cosmetics.

294
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:08,178
I can call the company,
see if I can get a track on him.

295
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:13,401
- Anything?
- Searched every cabin and shack. Nothing.

296
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:16,654
- Have them drop you back at the station.
- Okay, boss.

297
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:20,074
- Where you going?
- For a walk.

298
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:32,461
How you doing?

299
00:19:35,382 --> 00:19:38,259
People are saying that I killed Kara.

300
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:41,512
That's why there's a policeman outside.
So that I don't escape.

301
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:43,598
Hmm.

302
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:46,934
Did you? Kill Kara?

303
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:50,062
I don't know.

304
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:52,940
I don't think I did.

305
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:57,778
- Do you think I did?
- No.

306
00:19:57,946 --> 00:19:59,488
Why would you kill Kara?

307
00:20:00,532 --> 00:20:03,367
Yeah. Why would I kill her?

308
00:20:06,455 --> 00:20:09,290
But the thing is, I don't know.

309
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:12,460
I don't think I did...

310
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:13,669
...but I don't know.

311
00:20:13,837 --> 00:20:17,465
- Hey. Hey, where you going?
- Take your hands off of me.

312
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:19,508
- Don't make me tase you.
- Guys, come on.

313
00:20:19,676 --> 00:20:22,386
- Everybody, just take it down a notch.
- Uh, what's going on?

314
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:24,472
He was trying to sneak in to see her.

315
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:27,683
I was trying to see my girl.
I was just walking through.

316
00:20:27,851 --> 00:20:30,478
Nobody's allowed to see her right now.

317
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:34,190
Come on.

318
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:40,321
Wow.

319
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,990
- Are they gone?
- Yes.

320
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,702
I'm not ready to see anyone yet.

321
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:50,748
- You okay? You need me to get the nurse?
- No. No, no.

322
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:53,251
- Don't leave me alone.
- I won't.

323
00:20:56,922 --> 00:20:59,715
What was it in particular
that scared you just now, Nicole?

324
00:21:00,217 --> 00:21:01,842
I don't know.

325
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,349
I'm sorry.

326
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:12,270
It's okay. It's not your fault.

327
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:24,198
Rulon, we need to talk to you
about Kara Palmer. Let's go.

328
00:21:39,923 --> 00:21:42,883
Rigsby! Get up! Come on, get up!

329
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:56,439
Get him up. Let's go.

330
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:00,276
Nice job, guys.

331
00:22:51,536 --> 00:22:53,621
Daddy, listen.

332
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:06,008
What?

333
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:09,762
Yeah, yeah. I'll be there.

334
00:23:12,974 --> 00:23:15,518
So how is it you know Kara Palmer?

335
00:23:15,727 --> 00:23:18,479
This town's on my regular route,
and I stop here to eat.

336
00:23:18,647 --> 00:23:20,898
Hunting store's next door to the diner.

337
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:25,236
One day I walk in there, and a tight
little pair of buns caught my eye.

338
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:29,490
Boy meets girl. So I walk over
and I start up a conversation.

339
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:33,244
- What did you talk about?
- Offered her $10 to sit in my lap.

340
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:34,620
She said no.

341
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:38,499
But she said "no" in that kind of way
like I was lowballing her.

342
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:42,253
Not "no," like, to the general principle.

343
00:23:42,421 --> 00:23:45,172
I guess you could say
I've been courting her.

344
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:47,925
I'm through town, I stop by,
I give her some free stuff.

345
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:50,511
What did you expect from Kara in return?

346
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:53,389
I gave her a lot of stuff.

347
00:23:54,015 --> 00:23:58,519
So I'm thinking, eventually,
some form of sexual congress.

348
00:23:58,687 --> 00:23:59,854
And what did you get?

349
00:24:01,898 --> 00:24:04,942
- I disgust you, don't I?
- A little. Yeah.

350
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:07,361
You're pretty.

351
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:09,113
How's your lipstick supply?

352
00:24:12,325 --> 00:24:16,787
You beautiful people got no idea
what unattractive guys go through.

353
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:18,456
Don't I have a heart?

354
00:24:18,623 --> 00:24:22,793
Don't I long to be held, to be loved,
to be cherished?

355
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:24,879
Yes, I do.

356
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:33,721
So I gotta pay for a little human contact
every now and then. Shoot me.

357
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:38,017
- It's not my fault I look like this.
- It is, actually. With a low-carb diet...

358
00:24:38,185 --> 00:24:41,729
- ...and exercise, you could look different.
- I got a glandular problem.

359
00:24:41,897 --> 00:24:43,731
How heavy are you exactly?

360
00:24:46,067 --> 00:24:49,695
Two forty-five.
I've lost a lot of weight in the last year.

361
00:24:49,863 --> 00:24:52,656
You expected sexual favors from Kara.
What did you get?

362
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:56,410
She was a beautiful woman.

363
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:02,333
Nothing more beautiful
than a beautiful woman.

364
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:05,336
- What did you get from Kara?
- Nothing at all.

365
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:10,674
In France, they would have
called her a "coquette."

366
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:14,929
But I always held out high hopes.
I mean, there's always hope.

367
00:25:15,096 --> 00:25:16,430
There sure is.

368
00:25:19,809 --> 00:25:23,354
Suppose she never did put out for you.
How would you feel?

369
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:27,024
If I killed all the women
that had rejected me...

370
00:25:29,277 --> 00:25:31,070
...I'd have killed a lot of women.

371
00:25:31,238 --> 00:25:35,241
We can place you at the same bar where
Kara was last seen, the night of her murder.

372
00:25:35,408 --> 00:25:37,368
Heh, so were a whole boatload
of other people.

373
00:25:37,536 --> 00:25:40,371
Where were you between
1:30 and 7 a.m. that morning?

374
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:42,289
- My motel.
- Were you alone?

375
00:25:43,124 --> 00:25:44,959
- Yeah, I was.
- So you have no alibi.

376
00:25:45,126 --> 00:25:48,796
- Nope. Doesn't look good for me, does it?
- You seem fine with that.

377
00:25:49,297 --> 00:25:52,925
You know, I read that prosecutors
are not real happy with juries nowadays.

378
00:25:53,301 --> 00:25:56,136
Because those folks watch
a lot of crime shows on TV.

379
00:25:56,304 --> 00:25:58,764
And they walk in there
expecting every crime scene...

380
00:25:58,932 --> 00:26:02,601
...to have, like, DNA, hair, whatnot.

381
00:26:02,769 --> 00:26:08,065
And if that prosecutor does not hand them
the defendant's spit on a plate...

382
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:11,485
- ...not guilty.
- You saying you're innocent or careful?

383
00:26:11,945 --> 00:26:14,113
You'll never know.

384
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:31,505
He has no alibi, but we have no proof.
I can't find an angle to get at him.

385
00:26:31,673 --> 00:26:35,509
- He's shameless. He likes the attention.
- Maybe we should let Jane at him.

386
00:26:35,677 --> 00:26:38,512
Hey, Jane, wanna have a crack at him?

387
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,347
Jane?

388
00:26:40,515 --> 00:26:41,849
Oh, him...? Oh, let him go.

389
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:45,185
- Let him go?
- What for?

390
00:26:45,353 --> 00:26:49,106
- We had to fight to catch him.
- You're such policemen. Yes. Let him go.

391
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:51,984
- Set him free. He's telling the truth.
- You know this, how?

392
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:56,488
He liked Kara. Why would he kill her
and kidnap Nicole? Doesn't make any sense.

393
00:26:56,906 --> 00:27:00,284
Besides, he blushed
when he lied about his weight.

394
00:27:01,286 --> 00:27:04,204
Innocent.

395
00:27:04,372 --> 00:27:06,707
Kara, not quite as innocent
as she's been painted.

396
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:10,252
- By the word of a creep.
- An honest creep, whose stuff she took...

397
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:14,298
- ...knowing what kind of a man he was.
- Free eyeliner doesn't make her a whore.

398
00:27:14,466 --> 00:27:18,052
And a man blushing, embarrassed
by his weight, hardly makes him innocent.

399
00:27:18,219 --> 00:27:20,387
It makes him sensitive about his weight.

400
00:27:20,555 --> 00:27:23,807
I think he's a good prospect.
We should keep him close.

401
00:27:24,184 --> 00:27:28,062
- Hey, is that Kara's MP3 player?
- Yeah.

402
00:27:28,521 --> 00:27:30,272
What are you doing with it?

403
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:34,234
- Uh, listening to music. It's pretty good.
- That's evidence. You can't play with that.

404
00:27:34,402 --> 00:27:37,905
- Evidence of what? She likes music?
- It's in the log as physical evidence.

405
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:41,158
- It's evidence.
- Okay. What's with her?

406
00:27:41,326 --> 00:27:44,745
Seriously, if it's in the log, it's in the log.
You can't touch it.

407
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:54,421
Really? All right. Well, uh, ahem, I'm sorry.
I didn't realize it was a sacred thing.

408
00:27:54,589 --> 00:27:57,675
I'll put it right back.
You gonna release Rulon, or what?

409
00:27:57,842 --> 00:28:00,844
I don't want to.
But I don't have enough to hold him on.

410
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:03,847
Let him go.
We'll keep him under surveillance.

411
00:28:04,182 --> 00:28:06,016
Put that back.

412
00:28:08,770 --> 00:28:11,647
Rulon, you can go.
Sorry about the inconvenience.

413
00:28:14,734 --> 00:28:16,402
There it is.

414
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:55,983
Nicole.

415
00:28:58,278 --> 00:28:59,695
Hey.

416
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:02,072
You wanna get out of here?

417
00:29:08,163 --> 00:29:10,789
Put these on as quick as you can.

418
00:29:10,957 --> 00:29:11,999
Quick as you can.

419
00:29:24,679 --> 00:29:26,221
Hi.

420
00:29:32,854 --> 00:29:34,688
If I may?

421
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:37,691
Thank you.

422
00:29:43,406 --> 00:29:45,449
I'll be right back.

423
00:29:50,622 --> 00:29:52,247
Hey.

424
00:29:52,415 --> 00:29:53,874
Hey.

425
00:29:54,042 --> 00:29:55,709
Hey!

426
00:30:14,896 --> 00:30:18,565
There's nothing left to eat.
You cleaned us out this morning.

427
00:30:38,628 --> 00:30:40,254
Listen.

428
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:48,262
- Cars.
- The flow of them. It's like a hum.

429
00:30:49,305 --> 00:30:54,393
What if Nicole didn't hear water that night?
What if it was the flow of traffic?

430
00:30:54,561 --> 00:30:58,272
Then we should have been searching cabins
on this side of town. Near the highway.

431
00:30:58,439 --> 00:31:01,400
We'll split up.
I'll get a ranger, search the likely spots.

432
00:31:01,568 --> 00:31:03,694
You stay with Rulon.

433
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:10,409
Where are we going?

434
00:31:11,452 --> 00:31:13,579
You trust me, Nicole?

435
00:31:14,789 --> 00:31:16,456
Yes.

436
00:31:20,378 --> 00:31:23,130
I'm gonna help you remember
what happened to you that night.

437
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:26,300
- I don't wanna remember.
- You have to.

438
00:31:27,260 --> 00:31:31,722
Wherever you go, until you know the truth
of what happened, you'll be haunted.

439
00:31:32,307 --> 00:31:34,975
Until you see Kara's death redeemed,
you will be haunted.

440
00:31:35,143 --> 00:31:36,476
You have to know the truth.

441
00:31:50,617 --> 00:31:52,618
It makes me feel sad.

442
00:31:52,785 --> 00:31:55,746
It's the same music
that was playing in Kara's car that night.

443
00:31:56,122 --> 00:31:57,789
Yes.

444
00:31:59,667 --> 00:32:01,335
Yes. How did you know that?

445
00:32:01,878 --> 00:32:04,212
- Are you psychic?
- No.

446
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:05,839
These machines have clocks.

447
00:32:06,007 --> 00:32:09,009
They log in their memory
what was played when.

448
00:32:13,806 --> 00:32:16,350
Kara told you a secret, didn't she?

449
00:32:16,517 --> 00:32:20,228
A terrible secret
she'd been keeping from you.

450
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:24,316
But she had to tell you.
She had to be honest.

451
00:32:28,529 --> 00:32:30,864
- I'm gonna be sick.
- Okay.

452
00:32:40,291 --> 00:32:44,169
She said that I shouldn't marry Jason,
because he's no good.

453
00:32:44,337 --> 00:32:46,880
And I said she was wrong.

454
00:32:47,256 --> 00:32:50,759
And then she said
that she knows he's no good...

455
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:56,390
...because she and him
were sneaking around behind my back.

456
00:32:59,352 --> 00:33:01,269
Hooking up.

457
00:33:03,439 --> 00:33:05,148
I'm sorry.

458
00:33:19,497 --> 00:33:20,831
Nicole, then what happened?

459
00:33:22,333 --> 00:33:23,875
No.

460
00:33:25,586 --> 00:33:28,714
- No, I don't wanna remember any more.
- You must.

461
00:33:28,881 --> 00:33:31,258
No. I'm scared.

462
00:33:38,349 --> 00:33:40,183
I've been where you're going.

463
00:33:40,893 --> 00:33:43,103
I know how you feel.

464
00:33:43,646 --> 00:33:45,439
I know.

465
00:33:47,150 --> 00:33:49,568
But you have to be brave.

466
00:33:51,279 --> 00:33:53,030
I'm here.

467
00:33:53,448 --> 00:33:57,284
I won't let anything bad happen.
I promise.

468
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:06,793
Nicole, I'm sorry.

469
00:34:07,754 --> 00:34:10,130
I'm so sorry.

470
00:34:13,718 --> 00:34:15,135
Nicole, get back in the car.

471
00:34:15,303 --> 00:34:17,888
Go screw yourself!

472
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:20,766
Get in the car.

473
00:34:21,476 --> 00:34:25,645
Hey, mister, you looking for a good time?
Because my friend here is a cheap whore.

474
00:34:25,813 --> 00:34:28,440
- And I'm sure she'd be happy...
- Nicole.

475
00:34:40,119 --> 00:34:43,163
Kara died trying to save me.

476
00:34:47,001 --> 00:34:49,044
I'm being carried now.

477
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:08,897
I can hear the engine. It's vibrating.

478
00:35:09,065 --> 00:35:12,067
- Gasoline or diesel?
- Sounded like a diesel.

479
00:35:12,235 --> 00:35:14,903
Where is he taking you?
Is it a long journey?

480
00:35:15,071 --> 00:35:18,824
No. No, not long. Short.

481
00:35:19,075 --> 00:35:21,201
A bumpy road.

482
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:24,412
Agent Lisbon.

483
00:35:24,580 --> 00:35:27,999
Your man Jane just kidnapped
Nicole Gilbert from the hospital.

484
00:35:28,376 --> 00:35:30,544
- Oh, no.
- Oh, yes.

485
00:35:31,045 --> 00:35:34,965
And I'm not happy.
In fact, I'm mad as hell.

486
00:35:35,133 --> 00:35:36,383
You people are my guests.

487
00:35:36,551 --> 00:35:40,011
You can't come in here
and abduct my suspects.

488
00:35:40,179 --> 00:35:43,181
Sheriff, I will fix this.
Let me get on it right away.

489
00:35:43,349 --> 00:35:44,933
- Son of a bitch.
- What's up?

490
00:35:45,101 --> 00:35:48,353
Personnel issues.
Pick up your phone, damn it.

491
00:35:56,362 --> 00:35:58,280
We're stopping now.

492
00:36:01,242 --> 00:36:03,743
It's like an old shed.

493
00:36:05,037 --> 00:36:09,666
It's small and dark, and cold and dusty.

494
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:14,796
I'm scared.

495
00:36:15,673 --> 00:36:17,632
Somebody help me!

496
00:36:19,093 --> 00:36:21,386
- The door won't open. I can't get out.
- You will.

497
00:36:21,554 --> 00:36:23,388
- I can't get out.
- It's gonna be fine.

498
00:36:23,556 --> 00:36:26,266
The door will open. It will open.

499
00:36:26,434 --> 00:36:27,767
Is it bolted?

500
00:36:29,103 --> 00:36:30,520
Somebody help!

501
00:36:30,688 --> 00:36:32,105
No.

502
00:36:32,273 --> 00:36:35,483
- Chained?
- No, I don't think so.

503
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:39,779
I'm trapped. I'm gonna die.
I can't get out of here. I'm gonna die.

504
00:36:39,989 --> 00:36:43,950
Nicole, you can open it. It's your choice.
The door is unlocked if you want it to be.

505
00:36:44,118 --> 00:36:46,328
Open the door, Nicole. Open it.

506
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:59,799
- It's cold up here at night, huh?
- Yeah. And broiling during the day.

507
00:36:59,967 --> 00:37:02,219
Worst of both worlds.

508
00:37:06,557 --> 00:37:08,391
He's got a knife on me.

509
00:37:11,479 --> 00:37:12,646
No.

510
00:37:13,481 --> 00:37:15,941
He's trying to rape me,
but I won't let him.

511
00:37:25,701 --> 00:37:26,993
Where the hell are you?

512
00:37:27,161 --> 00:37:30,664
Nicole remembered everything.
She can describe the suspect.

513
00:37:30,831 --> 00:37:34,542
We're looking for a tall, well-built man,
with brown hair and glasses.

514
00:37:34,710 --> 00:37:36,419
- Mid-thirties.
- That's it?

515
00:37:36,587 --> 00:37:40,173
- That describes half the men in California.
- Yeah, that's it.

516
00:37:40,341 --> 00:37:42,842
But at least we know
it wasn't her that killed Kara.

517
00:37:44,637 --> 00:37:46,012
And it wasn't Rulon Farnes.

518
00:37:46,180 --> 00:37:49,975
Nice work. For this, you illegally
abducted her from the sheriff's custody?

519
00:37:50,142 --> 00:37:53,853
Yeah, I was gonna tell you about it.
But I figured, seeing that it's illegal...

520
00:37:54,021 --> 00:37:56,523
...best to keep you out of it,
so you have deniability.

521
00:37:56,691 --> 00:37:57,983
Oh, how considerate of you.

522
00:37:59,610 --> 00:38:03,697
Listen to me carefully,
and do exactly as I tell you.

523
00:38:03,864 --> 00:38:07,867
Take her back to the hospital right now,
and sincerely apologize to Sheriff Nelson.

524
00:38:14,250 --> 00:38:16,793
Wow, what was all that about?

525
00:38:18,087 --> 00:38:20,422
My bad karma.

526
00:38:22,174 --> 00:38:24,551
- How's she doing anyway?
- Who?

527
00:38:24,719 --> 00:38:27,220
That girl. Nicole. How's she holding up?

528
00:38:27,847 --> 00:38:29,556
Okay, considering.

529
00:38:29,724 --> 00:38:32,142
She remember anything yet?

530
00:38:33,269 --> 00:38:35,770
- We're doing what we can.
- Good.

531
00:38:37,815 --> 00:38:43,403
Is there anything else, anything specific
that you can remember about him?

532
00:38:46,240 --> 00:38:49,242
That's what he looked like.
That's all I remember.

533
00:38:49,410 --> 00:38:52,454
It doesn't matter how small it is.
Little things.

534
00:38:52,621 --> 00:38:55,707
Like what his voice sounded like
or what did he smelled like or...?

535
00:38:58,252 --> 00:39:00,295
Pineapple.

536
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:03,923
That's great.

537
00:39:04,925 --> 00:39:06,384
Is this the last place to check?

538
00:39:07,762 --> 00:39:10,221
- No, there's one more place.
- All right, let's go.

539
00:39:14,935 --> 00:39:17,645
- Hey.
- Pineapple.

540
00:39:17,813 --> 00:39:19,189
He smelled like pineapple.

541
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:21,691
Pineapple? What the hell? Go...

542
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:31,076
Okay. Good.

543
00:39:31,243 --> 00:39:34,329
Listen, tell Rigsby, Teresa needs his help.

544
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:41,002
Me? I'm at the Eagle Pine Lodge
off Route 6.

545
00:39:41,670 --> 00:39:43,129
Okay.

546
00:39:53,307 --> 00:39:57,227
Kyle, let's stay calm
and think this through.

547
00:39:57,603 --> 00:40:00,730
Heh. Think what through?

548
00:40:01,315 --> 00:40:05,610
I really don't wanna shoot you,
but I do have to take you into custody...

549
00:40:05,778 --> 00:40:08,571
...for killing Kara Palmer.
What are we gonna do about that?

550
00:40:11,951 --> 00:40:14,119
It's not like I set out to hurt anyone.

551
00:40:14,286 --> 00:40:16,037
I just wanted to talk to Nicole.

552
00:40:16,205 --> 00:40:18,164
Before she ran off and got married?

553
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:21,835
I've noticed her around town
for a long time.

554
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:26,673
I didn't want her marrying that guy Jason.
She's too good for him.

555
00:40:26,841 --> 00:40:31,344
Please, Kyle. I really and truly
do not wanna hurt you.

556
00:40:33,222 --> 00:40:35,014
You like your chances, do you?

557
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:49,904
Uh, Lisbon?

558
00:40:51,323 --> 00:40:52,782
Lisbon?

559
00:40:52,950 --> 00:40:54,701
- Lisbon?
- Shh!

560
00:40:57,329 --> 00:41:01,082
- You all right?
- Yeah. Did you call Rigsby?

561
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:05,003
Yeah, he's on his way.
Listen, I have an idea.

562
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:13,428
Lisbon, be careful.

563
00:41:27,693 --> 00:41:29,444
Drop it.

564
00:41:30,905 --> 00:41:33,448
Really. Drop it.

565
00:41:34,074 --> 00:41:35,992
On your knees.

566
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:39,078
Your hands. Come on.

567
00:41:39,246 --> 00:41:40,914
Let's go.

568
00:41:47,546 --> 00:41:49,422
Nice work, Jane.

569
00:41:55,804 --> 00:41:57,514
I was hoping I'd find you here.

570
00:41:57,890 --> 00:42:00,433
Yeah, we're, uh,
just about to hit the road.

571
00:42:02,394 --> 00:42:04,145
Thank you.

572
00:42:06,649 --> 00:42:08,233
It's okay.

573
00:42:12,655 --> 00:42:17,283
You know, uh, eventually,
you'll start to remember the good things.

574
00:42:19,954 --> 00:42:21,371
Yeah.

575
00:42:24,708 --> 00:42:27,877
- Goes without saying.
- You're welcome.

576
00:42:29,046 --> 00:42:30,838
You ready to go?

577
00:42:32,883 --> 00:42:35,468
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

578
00:42:44,061 --> 00:42:47,522
Hey, can you believe
he fell for that old cell-phone gag?

579
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:50,650
Old cell-phone gag?
I invented that right there and then.

580
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:52,944
- Rather brilliantly, I thought.
- Oh, please.

581
00:42:53,112 --> 00:42:54,904
I've seen that done a dozen times.

582
00:42:55,406 --> 00:42:57,490
- What do you mean? Where?
- On TV.

583
00:42:57,658 --> 00:43:01,369
Oh, on TV.
Well, anything can happen on TV.

584
00:43:04,164 --> 00:43:08,626
The question is,
where have you seen that done in real life?

